{
  "bridge_text": "那棵大树在寒风中低声吟唱，莉娜紧了紧红色的斗篷，终于下定决心，推开了那扇仿佛一直在等待她的树洞大门。",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "text": "莉娜深吸一口气，穿过树洞的阴影，发现里面竟有一道盘旋向下的楼梯。在最高的那一级台阶上，坐着一只穿着补丁绿背心的老灰狐狸。他自称莫斯克，用沙哑如枯叶般的声音告诉莉娜，这棵树不是用来探访的，让她赶紧回家，忘记那阵嗡嗡声。莉娜却摇摇头，坚定地说，她无法忘记尚未听到的秘密。"
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s1"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "While Mosk keeps his reasons hidden behind that grumpy frown, his eyes linger on the path ahead. The old fox turns, ready to show Lina what lies beneath the roots.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Though she stood firm, Mosk only narrowed his eyes, his tail twitching against the bark. The tree remained silent, waiting for him to decide if this girl was a nuisance or a guest. With a huff that ruffled his whiskers, he finally turned away from the doorway."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "With the name Mosk echoing softly between them, Lina watched as the old fox turned his gaze toward the wooden door. The path forward remained just as mysterious as the humming that pulled her deeper into the roots.",
  "resume_strategy": "skip",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed at the door. Lina reached into her pocket and pulled out the last apple of the season. She set it on the step between them and said, this is for the trouble of walking me down. Mosk stared at the apple for a long time. Then he stood up, tied his vest, and stepped onto the first stair without a word."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "Lina knew that a gift offered with a kind heart often opens paths that stealthy feet cannot. With the apple left behind on the wooden step, she followed Mosk down into the deepening shadows.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk stared at the apple for a long time, his golden eyes unblinking. Then he stood up, tied his vest, and stepped onto the first stair without a word. Lina followed close behind, her boots making no sound against the hollow wood as they descended into the cool, quiet heart of the tree."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "Just like that soft, green blanket of moss keeps the earth cozy, the firefly queen rested in the quiet dark of the hollow tree. Mosk watched her, his heart heavy with the memory of a winter long past.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "At the bottom of the stairs, the humming softened into a melody. There lay the firefly, as large as a robin, resting upon a thick bed of velvet-green moss that cushioned her tired wings. Her glow flickered, nearly spent. Mosk’s whiskers trembled as he looked at her. He whispered that she had been his dearest friend, but one winter, he had arrived too late with her medicine. Ever since, he had guarded this hollow tree, too ashamed to look her in the eye."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s4"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "With Mosk settled on that high step in his green vest, Lina stood her ground, waiting to see if he would truly turn her away from the mystery of the humming.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Inside the hollow tree, a curl of stairs spiraled downward into the gloom. At the very top step sat Mosk, an old grey fox wearing a patched green vest. His voice, dry as autumn leaves, warned Lina that the tree was no place for visitors and she should return home. Yet, Lina shook her head, insisting that she could never forget a song she had not yet heard."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "With the taste of autumn apples still lingering in the air, Mosk slowly led the way down the creaking staircase. His paws moved softly as he descended into the heart of the hollow tree.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk stared at the apple for a long time. Then he stood up, tied his vest, and stepped onto the first stair without a word. The wood groaned beneath his weight, echoing into the shadows below where the air grew thick with the scent of damp earth and ancient magic."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "While the firefly’s light flickers like a dying ember, the shadows in the hollow tree hold their breath to see what happens next. With Mosk watching closely, Lina reaches out to help the tiny queen.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "Mosk's whiskers trembled as he looked at the dim glow. He had been her friend once, he whispered, and one winter long ago he had failed to bring her medicine in time. He had been guarding the tree ever since, ashamed to face her, hoping for a chance to make things right."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "Lina knelt and asked the firefly queen what she needed. A drop of warm milk and a kind word, said the queen, that was all medicine ever was. Mosk fetched the milk in a thimble and laid his paw beside hers. The queen's glow steadied. The humming inside the tree turned into a tune Lina had not heard before — and Mosk, for the first time in years, hummed along."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s4"
}

